1
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The Breakfast is a drama, comedy film directed by Peter Sheridan.

2
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Curly Mulligan is the pupil who brings the
headmaster a full fry-up every morning.

3
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:42,000
When the head finds a hair in his breakfast, all hell breaks loose.

4
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Curly Mulligan, played by Gavin Dowdall.

5
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Brother Ledwidge, played by Frank McDonald.

6
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Smiley Byrne, played by Patrick Hyland.

7
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Skinny Palmer, played by Kevin James.

8
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Boy Buttering Bread, played by Gerard Cannon.

9
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Boy Cutting Bread, played by Peter Rogers.

10
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Breakfast on Pluto is a 2005 comedy-drama film directed by Neil Jordan from a screenplay he
co-wrote with Patrick McCabe, based on McCabe's 1998 novel of the same name.

11
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Set during the Troubles in the 1970s, the film stars Cillian Murphy as a transgender woman
foundling who leaves her small Irish town for London in search of her long-lost mother.

12
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Stephen Rea, Brendan Gleeson and Liam Neeson also star.

13
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:42,000
The film explores themes of boarding school, breakfast,
dark comedy, brotherhood, young boy.

14
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:54,000
The tone is lighthearted and dark and emotional.
